[natasha@ststor01 ~]$  which command do i enter for this : sudo yum install -y $PACKAGE || sudo dnf install -y $PACKAGE

If your storage server is Ubuntu instead of RHEL:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y $PACKAGE

Your storage server is:

CentOS Stream 9

It is RHEL-based, so you should not use apt.

For CentOS Stream 9, use either dnf or yum. Since CentOS 9 uses dnf underneath, the preferred command is:

sudo dnf install -y $PACKAGE

However, this command is also fine:

sudo yum install -y $PACKAGE || sudo dnf install -y $PACKAGE

Why?

yum install -y $PACKAGE tries first.

If yum fails, || runs:

sudo dnf install -y $PACKAGE
On CentOS Stream 9, yum is usually a compatibility link to dnf, so both work.

For your Jenkins job, I recommend using the simpler:

sudo dnf install -y $PACKAGE

Then run your Jenkins build with:

PACKAGE=vim-enhanced

After it finishes, verify on ststor01:

rpm -q vim-enhanced

Expected output will look like:

vim-enhanced-9.x.x.el9.x86_64

One more thing: because Jenkins connects as natasha, make sure natasha has passwordless sudo. Test:

sudo -n dnf install -y vim-enhanced

If it returns a sudo password error, Jenkins will fail even with the correct SSH setup.

[natasha@ststor01 ~]$ rpm -q vim-enhanced
vim-enhanced-8.2.2637-33.el9.x86_64

