A developer joins the company.

A Jenkins job can prepare a server with:

java
maven
nodejs
docker
kubectl
terraform
4. CI/CD pipeline dependency installation

Suppose an application requires:

java-17
maven
docker

Before deployment, Jenkins ensures the deployment server has everything needed.

Example pipeline:

Developer pushes code
          |
          ↓
      GitHub
          |
          ↓
       Jenkins
          |
          ↓
 Install dependencies
          |
          ↓
 Build application
          |
          ↓
 Deploy to servers
5. Standardization across environments

Companies usually have:

Development servers
Testing servers
Staging servers
Production servers

Automation ensures all environments have the same packages.

Example:

Without automation:

Production:
Java 17 installed

Testing:
Java 11 installed

Development:
Java 21 installed

This causes "works on my machine" problems.

With Jenkins:

install-packages
PACKAGE=java-17

Every server gets the same version.

